"default shell, you can do it by editing either ``~/.profile`` or ``~/."
"bash_profile`` and adding the following line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/shell-commands.rst:48
msgid ""
"If you use Zsh, you can either edit ``~/.zprofile`` and add the code above, "
"or for supporting both, Bash and Zsh, you can first edit ``~/.profile`` and "
"add the code above, then edit ``~/.zprofile`` and add the following line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/shell-commands.rst:56
msgid ""
"If you don't know the difference between the two, check out `this page "
"<https://serverfault.com/questions/261802/what-are-the-functional-"
"differences-between-profile-bash-profile-and-bashrc>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/shell-commands.rst:58
msgid ""
"Now that is done, or if ``$HOME/.local/bin/`` was already exported to your "
"PATH environmental variable, you can create the symlinks by opening your "
"system terminal app and paste these commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/shell-commands.rst:68
msgid ""
"After everything's done, just restart your session (log out and log back in) "
"and you're good to go."
msgstr ""

